1
00:00:00,359 --> 00:00:03,429
(Leonard:)Well, what if we go
around the university

2
00:00:03,429 --> 00:00:04,599
(Leonard:)and just get
the patent ourselves?

3
00:00:04,596 --> 00:00:05,926
(Leonard:)We can't.
It says on their Web site,

4
00:00:05,931 --> 00:00:07,501
(Howard:)as long as we work there,
they have

5
00:00:07,499 --> 00:00:10,769
(Howard:)a controlling ownership
of anything we come up with.

6
00:00:10,769 --> 00:00:13,299
(Sheldon:)Great, so they own
my idea for a T-shirt

7
00:00:13,305 --> 00:00:16,545
(Sheldon:)that says
“Dumb as a Bag of Geologists.”

8
00:00:19,845 --> 00:00:22,345
(Leonard:)Well, our choices are we
do this with the university

9
00:00:22,347 --> 00:00:23,617
(Leonard:)or we don't do it at all.

10
00:00:23,615 --> 00:00:26,515
(Howard:)Either way, I get nothing.

11
00:00:26,518 --> 00:00:28,848
(Leonard:)Or, if we ended up
making money from this,

12
00:00:28,854 --> 00:00:31,654
(Leonard:)Sheldon and I could split
our shares with you.

13
00:00:31,657 --> 00:00:33,527
(Sheldon:)To be clear,

14
00:00:33,525 --> 00:00:35,025
(Sheldon:)Leonard is referring
to the gyroscope,

15
00:00:35,027 --> 00:00:37,597
(Sheldon:)not the T-shirt and mugs.

16
00:00:37,596 --> 00:00:40,526
Oh! Now they own the mugs.

17
00:00:41,733 --> 00:00:44,063
(Howard:)I guess that is
a way around this.

18
00:00:44,069 --> 00:00:46,369
(Howard:)You guys would be cool
doing it like that?

19
00:00:46,371 --> 00:00:48,171
(Leonard:)Of course, we can split
any profits three ways.

20
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:49,143
(Sheldon:)I'm fine with that.

21
00:00:49,141 --> 00:00:50,911
(Howard:)Okay, great.

22
00:00:50,909 --> 00:00:54,609
(Sheldon:)It sounds like a, uh,
contract might be in order.

23
00:00:57,449 --> 00:00:59,549
(Leonard:)Sure, we could write
something up.

